      starterCode: "import math\n\ndef stable_softmax(row):\n    m = max(row)\n    exps = [math.exp(v - m) for v in row]\n    return [e / sum(exps) for e in exps]\n\n# temperature scaling: divide logits by T before the softmax\nlogits = [2.0, 1.0, 0.1]\nfor T in (0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 10.0):\n    scaled = [v / T for v in logits]\n    print('T=%4.1f ->' % T, ['%.4f' % p for p in stable_softmax(scaled)])\n\n# جرّب: T صغيرة جداً تقرب التوزيع من one-hot (ثقة زائدة)، وT كبيرة تسطحه نحو المنتظم.\n# try: very small T approaches one-hot (overconfident); large T flattens toward uniform.\n# جرّب: احسب cross-entropy للتوزيع المنتظم مع التسميات [0, 2] وقارنه بـ 1.4979.\n# try: compute cross-entropy of the uniform distribution with labels [0, 2] and compare with 1.4979.\n",
